        "title": "fix(slack): add timeout to startup auth.test requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users starting a Slack account could wait indefinitely when the startup `auth.test` call stalled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSlack startup now bounds the boot-time `auth.test` wait with the existing shared timeout helper and keeps the current degraded startup path when that identity check fails. The change is limited to startup identity validation and does not alter Slack send, upload, or read lookup behavior.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA stalled Slack identity check no longer prevents the Slack provider from reaching the existing degraded startup path and logging the same required-mention warning.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/provider.auth-test-token.test.ts`\n- Result: 1 test file passed, 8 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n- Autoreview attempted with `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD`; the local Codex review engine exited before returning structured findings, so no clean autoreview result is claimed here.\n",
